{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787201891405983001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"sticky-genetic-narwhal","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"418f0d683eb2c734a353264cbe652bffe99645a959854ed2db7a37c484fde310","event_uuid":"896455f8-fc36-4a04-a1f0-b9d20d349c45","position":{"commit_sha":"785f0ded5a43bc340ca2f15ac91bfa181b6e0aae","position":"1787197298960645001-896455f8-fc36-4a04-a1f0-b9d20d349c45"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"22affd196d5ebaeaeaa47c8cd6070ab9f5e07fbec33407c22614af74600f84d7","event_uuid":"d5d22159-f260-4b89-8e13-bd05ba97fea9","position":{"commit_sha":"cb248c5b8f91eb34df80f0ca8626db681fee4328","position":"1787197307099328001-d5d22159-f260-4b89-8e13-bd05ba97fea9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1b9e5dc586e9fd0dbe53ae8d97c1c9848b65b250ea2bc6927de7bc6638b1f679","event_uuid":"51ecc078-67f0-4e65-b8cc-aeb294b8c8db","position":{"commit_sha":"5f6d4fb9df92cc3646ef042628e7596edd971279","position":"1787197356338503001-51ecc078-67f0-4e65-b8cc-aeb294b8c8db"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787197298960645001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d5d22159-f260-4b89-8e13-bd05ba97fea9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"559b-b7cd-6552-437d"},{"link_uuid":"51ecc078-67f0-4e65-b8cc-aeb294b8c8db","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3a52-2d79-320d-4fed"}],"description":"## Current state — THIS MACHINE IS RUNNING WITHOUT AUTO-UPDATES\nThe hourly main-tracking updater was PAUSED on 2026-08-20 by operator decision, to stop it breaking\nin-flight work:\n\n```\nlaunchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.navapbc.rebar-dev-update      # what was run\nlaunchctl list | grep rebar-dev-update                           # now returns nothing\n```\n\nUntil this ticket is resolved, the global `rebar`/`rebar-mcp` on this host **no longer tracks\n`origin/main`** and will drift. That is a deliberate, temporary trade — but it is a standing\nregression in the environment, and this ticket owns undoing it safely.\n\n## The defect\n`~/.local/bin/rebar-dev-update.sh` (host-local, NOT in this repository) ends every run — the publish\npath AND the no-change path — with `prune_releases()`, which unconditionally `rm -rf`s every release\ndirectory that `current` does not point at, with no check for live processes.\n\nThe published runtime is an EDITABLE install: the release venv's site-packages contains only\n`_editable_impl_nava_rebar.pth` holding `<release>/src`, so a running interpreter resolves\nnot-yet-imported modules from that directory AT IMPORT TIME. rebar also imports lazily — the\nconfirmed case is `commit_impact` at `_commands/close_precheck.py:283`, inside\n`_check_file_impact_vs_diff`, which runs LATE in a close, after the minutes-long completion-verifier\nLLM gate. That is a multi-minute window in which the backing directory can vanish.\n\n## Evidence — two independent in-the-wild occurrences\n1. **2026-08-19**, original report, traced on `frangible-irongray-adouri` (closed as a duplicate of\n   `shady-blueblack-whale`). Log timeline: `d83fb4f6` published 17:25:18, `0b851c81` published\n   19:18:01 pruning `d83fb4f6`, failure reported 19:55:13 quoting a traceback rooted at the deleted\n   path. Reproduced offline character-for-character: import the parent package, `rmtree` the tree,\n   trigger the lazy import; negative control with the tree intact imports fine.\n2. **2026-08-20**, during this session, on a DIFFERENT release hash. A `rebar transition … closed`\n   died with\n   `ImportError: cannot import name 'commit_impact' from 'rebar._engine_support'` naming\n   `.../releases/d6841983c6…84448/…`. State captured immediately after: `releases/` contained\n   exactly ONE directory, `b91f8f6830…86589`; `current` pointed at it; the path in the traceback was\n   gone. The close FAILED and left the ticket `in_progress`, and a naive caller reading the exit\n   code would have believed it succeeded. Retrying against the fresh release then worked.\n\nNote both occurrences involved NO `uv tool install --force` — an ordinary scheduled prune is\nsufficient. That matters for `shady-blueblack-whale`, which is tracing the same class from the uv\ntrigger; a reproduction harness can be driven by a plain directory removal.\n\n## The hard constraint — why the obvious fixes are wrong\nThis host uses rebar **heavily and continually**: multiple concurrent agents, each running gates and\ncloses that take minutes. Any remedy must survive that, and the two naive options both fail:\n\n* **\"Never prune a release with live referencing processes.\"** Under continuous use there may never\n  be a moment with no live process, so releases accumulate without bound.\n* **\"Prune aggressively, accept the breakage.\"** That is today's behaviour, and it silently fails\n  closes.\n\nAnd unbounded accumulation is not hypothetical here: `masonic-abeyant-stagbeetle` (P1, closed\n2026-08-19) was a root-disk-pressure incident on the review-bot host, where the only thing bounding a\ngrowing store failed to engage until 93.3% disk used. A retention policy that never reclaims\nrecreates that incident. **The remedy must both stop deleting live releases AND keep reclaiming\nspace under continuous load.** Solving one at the expense of the other is not a fix.\n\nNote also that making the install non-editable does NOT by itself solve this: the prune deletes the\nwhole release directory including its `.venv`, so a copied package inside it disappears too. The\nproblem is deleting a directory a live process is executing from, not the editable indirection\nspecifically.\n\n## Candidate approaches (to be chosen on evidence, not assumed)\n- **Bounded retention**: keep the previous N releases (or any younger than T), so a running process\n  always has a grace window, with N/T sized against the longest realistic operation (a close with the\n  LLM completion verifier — measure it rather than guess).\n- **Liveness check with a bounded override**: skip pruning a release with live referencing processes,\n  but cap total retained releases/bytes; on breaching the cap, ALERT rather than delete a live\n  release, so the failure mode is a warning instead of a broken run.\n- **Publish-time indirection**: have the launcher resolve and pin a release for the process lifetime\n  so a prune cannot invalidate an in-flight resolution.\n- Some combination; defence in depth is acceptable if each layer is justified.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] **The updater is RE-ENABLED on this host and confirmed running** — `launchctl list` shows\n      `com.navapbc.rebar-dev-update` again, and a forced run\n      (`launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.navapbc.rebar-dev-update`) completes successfully.\n      This ticket is not done while the host is still drifting from `origin/main`.\n- [ ] A long-running `rebar` operation spanning at least one updater cycle COMPLETES successfully\n      while the updater is active — demonstrated, not argued. The natural probe is a real close\n      (whose LLM completion verifier takes minutes) with a forced update fired mid-run.\n- [ ] Disk usage remains BOUNDED under continuous rebar use: releases do not accumulate without\n      limit when operations are always in flight. State the bound (count or bytes) and show it\n      holding, so this does not recreate the `masonic-abeyant-stagbeetle` disk-pressure incident.\n- [ ] When the two goals genuinely conflict — a release cannot be reclaimed because it is in use and\n      the retention bound is reached — the behaviour is an explicit ALERT, not a silent deletion and\n      not a silent unbounded grow. Name where that alert surfaces.\n- [ ] The chosen mechanism and its rationale are documented in\n      `docs/local-env-main-tracking.local.md` (git-ignored, host-local), including how to pause and\n      resume, so the next operator does not rediscover this.\n- [ ] The failure signature is recorded somewhere a future reader will find it: an `ImportError`\n      naming a module that demonstrably exists in the source tree, with a path under\n      `~/.local/state/rebar-dev/releases/` that no longer exists, means a pruned-mid-run release —\n      not a packaging defect. Two sessions have now mis-diagnosed this as a packaging bug.\n\n## Scope note\nThe defective script `~/.local/bin/rebar-dev-update.sh` is HOST-LOCAL and outside this repository, so\nthe fix may land with no repo file impact. If investigation shows rebar itself should participate\n(for example a launcher that pins a resolved release for the process lifetime), that is a distinct\nin-repo change and should be filed separately rather than absorbed here.\n\nRelated: `shady-blueblack-whale` traces the same mechanism under the `uv tool install --force`\ntrigger; `frangible-irongray-adouri` (closed duplicate) carries the original traced RCA;\n`masonic-abeyant-stagbeetle` is the disk-pressure incident that constrains the retention side.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","3a52-2d79-320d-4fed"],["relates_to","559b-b7cd-6552-437d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"df15-4d58-1e8c-447c","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Hourly updater prunes the release directory out from under running rebar processes; updater currently PAUSED on this host","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["896455f8-fc36-4a04-a1f0-b9d20d349c45","d5d22159-f260-4b89-8e13-bd05ba97fea9","51ecc078-67f0-4e65-b8cc-aeb294b8c8db"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787201891405983001,"uuid":"d2295c0e-802f-4b9c-922e-f5f0b184156e"}